{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 7, :comments ["<b>A tender ox.</b> To cook quickly. Here Rashi explained: to feed them three tongues, to inform them that he slaughtered three animals for them — in mustard, but not in pepper, as we say in Eruvin, unlike the custom of the earlier generations, who did not have pepper. And why tongues? Because they were in a hurry to go on their way and could not wait until the animal was skinned." "<b>And he hastened to make it.</b> A term of preparation."], :book :genesis, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 18, :notes {0 "The bracketed word כדורות (generations) appears to be a variant reading for the text; translated as 'custom of the earlier generations.'"}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:04:36.840142860Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}